; A member/method access whose name does NOT exist on a CONCRETE resolved
; struct must FAIL LOUDLY, not silently read field 0. Before the emit-time
; guard, `b.nonexistent()` on a Box emitted `extractvalue Box, 0` — the first
; field (value) — so a typo'd method silently returned the wrong value. The
; guard (Emitter.scaly::emit_member_access_chain) traps when a non-method,
; non-variant hop has a VOID result and its parent maps to a sized concrete
; struct. Only viable after glob-type-disambiguation stopped the glob-
; ambiguity path from relying on the field-0 fallback.
;
; ★Since 2026-09-03 this shape is caught EARLIER and better: an unresolved hop
; FOLLOWED BY AN ARGS TUPLE is report_unresolved_method_call#'s hard rc-4, with
; a file:line:col the emitter's guard could never give (it has no source
; location, which is why exit 16 printed a bare name). The emitter guard is NOT
; redundant — it still covers the READ form, `let x b.nonexistent`, where there
; is no args tuple and nothing for the planner's call detection to key on.
; xfail: method not found: nonexistent in type Box

define Box
(
    value: int
)
{
    function val(this: Box) returns int
        value
}

function main() returns int
{
    let b Box(5)
    return b.nonexistent()
}
